%% Unique Jersey Wholesale — End-to-End Operational Lifecycle
%% Verified across 5 role scopes and PostgreSQL database transaction locks
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Salesman as Salesman (/salesman)
  actor Admin as Operations Admin (/admin)
  actor Warehouse as Warehouse Manager
  actor Driver as Delivery Partner (/delivery)
  actor Accountant as Accountant (/finance)

  Salesman->>Admin: 1. Create B2B Order (Catalog, Pricing Bands, Line Quantities)
  Note over Admin: Review order parameters & customer credit limit
  Admin->>Warehouse: 2. Approve Order & Trigger Initial Allocations
  Note over Warehouse: Pessimistic lockForUpdate() on line items, physical verification
  Warehouse->>Driver: 3. Pack Confirmed Inventory & Assign Route Dispatch
  Note over Driver: Pickup items, transit to store, recipient signature
  Driver->>Admin: 4. Complete Delivery & Upload Signed Proof (Magic-Byte Validated)
  Admin->>Accountant: 5. Transition to Fulfilled Status
  Note over Accountant: Generate tax invoice, double-entry journal lines, receivables aging
  Accountant-->>Salesman: 6. Order Settled & General Ledger Audited
